Q: react_native_video/RCTVideoManager.swift:7: Fatal error: Unexpectedly found nil while implicitly unwrapping an Optional value A: <p><strong>I solved the issue by following these steps:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><p>navigate to: node_modules/react-native-video/ios/Video/RCTVideoManager.swift</p>
</li>
<li><p>Replace this portion of code:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>override func view() -&gt; UIView {
        return RCTVideo(eventDispatcher: (RCTBridge.current().eventDispatcher() as! RCTEventDispatcher))
     }
</code></pre>
<p>with this:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>   override func view() -&gt; UIView {
    return RCTVideo(eventDispatcher: nil)
}
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>After replacing clear all issues and clean build folder in xcode (run the code again crash &amp; error will disappear).</p>
</li>
<li><p>after running successfully hit this cmd (npx patch-package react-native-video) it will create the patch file and error will be removed forever</p>
</li>
</ol>

Q: How to find out carrier&#39;s name when using MVNO? (i want the one written in notification Bar) A: <p>If you are struggling with <code>getNetworkOperatorName()</code> returning the <strong>host</strong> carrier (e.g., T-Mobile) instead of the <strong>MVNO</strong> (e.g., Mint Mobile), it is because Android is prioritizing the network broadcast over the SIM record.</p>
<p>To reliably get the name shown in the notification bar (which is usually the <strong>SPN</strong> or Service Provider Name), you need to check the SIM's specific records.</p>
<p><strong>The Hierarchy of Display Names:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>Carrier Config Override:</strong> (Highest priority) A name hardcoded by the OS/Carrier Config for that specific MCC/MNC + GID.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>SPN (Service Provider Name):</strong> Stored in the SIM file <code>EF_SPN</code>. This is the &quot;Marketing Name&quot; of the MVNO.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>PNN (PLMN Network Name):</strong> Stored in <code>EF_PNN</code>.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Network Operator:</strong> (Lowest priority) The broadcasted name from the tower (MNO).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Solution Code:</strong> You should attempt to read the <strong>SIM Operator Name</strong> first. If you are targeting Android 5.1+ (API 22), use <code>SubscriptionManager</code> to ensure you get the name for the <em>correct</em> SIM slot.</p>
<p>Java</p>
<pre><code>// For API 22+ (The modern way)
SubscriptionManager subManager = (SubscriptionManager) context.getSystemService(Context.TELEPHONY_SUBSCRIPTION_SERVICE);
// Permission check omitted for brevity (READ_PHONE_STATE)
List&lt;SubscriptionInfo&gt; subInfoList = subManager.getActiveSubscriptionInfoList();

if (subInfoList != null &amp;&amp; !subInfoList.isEmpty()) {
    for (SubscriptionInfo info : subInfoList) {
        // This returns the Display Name (usually SPN) shown in the Status Bar
        CharSequence carrierName = info.getDisplayName(); 
        Log.d(&quot;Carrier&quot;, &quot;Slot &quot; + info.getSimSlotIndex() + &quot;: &quot; + carrierName);
    }
}

// Fallback for older devices (The legacy way)
TelephonyManager manager = (TelephonyManager)context.getSystemService(Context.TELEPHONY_SERVICE);
String carrierName = manager.getSimOperatorName(); // Try obtaining the SPN

if (carrierName == null || carrierName.isEmpty()) {
    // Fallback to the network operator (e.g. T-Mobile) if SPN is missing
    carrierName = manager.getNetworkOperatorName();
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Why this still fails for some MVNOs:</strong> Some MVNOs (especially lighter MVNOs or IoT SIMs) do not properly program the <code>EF_SPN</code> file on their SIM cards. If that file is empty, Android has no choice but to display the Host MNO name.</p>
<p>In the IoT/Embedded space, this gets even more complex with <strong>Multi-IMSI SIMs</strong>, where the profile switches dynamically. This causes the &quot;Carrier Name&quot; to change based on which profile is currently active (e.g., switching from a French profile to a US profile).</p>
<p><em>Disclaimer: I work at Spenza, where we solve these connectivity mapping issues for global IoT fleets. We wrote a guide on the technical difference between <a href="https://spenza.com/esim/what-is-iccid-number/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">IMSI and MSISDN identities here</a>.</em></p>

Q: Codeigniter: Load model and controller result in Helper A: <p>My recommended adjustments:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>There is no need to declare <code>$this-&gt;data</code> a class property called <code>data</code>. This payload is going to be passed to the view being loaded and the original class property will never be accessed again. Just declare a local variable. To be honest, I don't know that you need to declare a local <code>$data</code> variable either, just pass a freshly populated associative array to the view loader.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Helper functions shouldn't ever need to call a model or a library. Wrapping CodeIgniter's native form helpers inside of your own helper probably isn't providing more economy/elegance. I'd just be writing those form field generators directly in the view.</p>
</li>
<li><p>When you strip out the model call and instead pass in the 2d payload as a function parameter, and move the CI helper calls to the view, the only thing that your helper is actually doing is re-inventing PHP's native <code>array_column()</code> function.  That is such a small process, you can squeeze that into your controller so that the form helpers in the view can instantly digest it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>class HR extends MX_Controller
{

    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct();
        $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('admin/hr/hr_model');
    }

    public function index()
    {
        $this-&gt;load-&gt;view('hr/index', [
            'positions' =&gt; array_column(
                $this-&gt;hr_model-&gt;get_positions(),
                'label',   /* element value (to be visible text of &lt;option&gt; tag) */
                'position' /* element key (to be value attribute of &lt;option&gt; tag) */
            ),
        ]);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>View:</p>
<pre class="lang-php-template prettyprint-override"><code>if ($positions) {
    echo form_open();
        echo form_dropdown('positions', $positions);
    echo form_close();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Relevant reading:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79695068/2943403">How to use query result set data in CodeIgniter's form_dropdown() helper function</a></li>
<li><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79835285/2943403">Present database table values as dropdown field options in CodeIgniter</a></li>
</ul>
